[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:52. A Pretty Carpet]
[00:00.820]Passage 52 | 文章五十二
[00:02.835]A pretty carpet. | 一块漂亮的地毯。
[00:05.505]We have just moved into a new house. | 我们刚搬进一所新房子。
[00:09.995]And I have been working hard all morning. | 我整个上午都在努力工作。
[00:13.645]I have been trying to get my new room in order. | 我一直努力把我的新房间整理好。
[00:18.460]This has not been easy because I own over a thousand books. | 这并不容易，因为我拥有一千多本书。
[00:25.185]To make matters worse, the room is rather small. | 更糟的是，房间相当小。
[00:29.605]So I have temporarily put my books on the floor. | 所以我暂时把书都放在了地板上。
[00:34.425]At the moment, they cover every inch of floor space. | 目前，它们占据了每一寸地板空间。
[00:39.855]And I actually have to walk on them to get in or out of the room. | 我甚至不得不踩着它们进出房间。
[00:45.550]A short while ago, my sister helped me to carry one of my old bookcases up the stairs. | 不久前，我妹妹帮我把一个旧书柜搬上了楼。
[00:54.875]She went into my room and got a big surprise when she saw all those books on the floor. | 她走进我的房间，看到地板上摆满了书，大吃一惊。
[01:02.750]"This is the prettiest carpet I have ever seen," she said. | “这是我见过的最漂亮的地毯，”她说。
[01:08.355]She gazed at it for some time, then added, | 她盯着它看了一会儿，然后补充道：
[01:12.970]"You don't need bookcases at all. | “你根本不需要书柜。
[01:16.445]You can sit here in your spare time and read the carpet." | 你可以在空闲时间坐在这里看地毯。”